  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Friday)\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nScattered showers and isolated storms are expected to be ongoing \nacross NE OK Saturday morning with a slow expansion eastward \nthrough early afternoon. Most guidance favors a decrease in precip\ncoverage through Saturday afternoon before showers and storms \ndevelop again Saturday evening and spread east and southeastward\nthrough the day Sunday. Higher precip chances will continue north\nof Interstate 40 through the day Saturday with a more broad\nrainfall footprint Saturday night into Sunday. Overall precip\namounts are forecast to remain light with little to no impact to\nthe ongoing drought conditions. The extent and duration of the\nthicker cloud cover will influence temperatures on both Saturday\nand Sunday, however expect temperatures remaining above seasonal\nnormals through the weekend.\n\nUpper ridge axis remains centered through the forecast area on\nMonday with very low rain chances and above normal temperatures\ncontinuing. The pattern transitions on Tuesday as a stronger mid\nlevel trough moves into the southwest CONUS and interacts with the\nremnants of tropical system Polo. Uncertainty increases\nsubstantially regarding the evolution of the resultant storm\nsystem with both timing and resultant weather impacts both in\nquestion. The general pattern of favorably, and possibly\nprolonged, synoptic scale lift interacting with a plume of deep\nmid level tropical moisture does favor high precip chances ahead\nof the advance mid level trough. Expect precip chances for mid to\nlate next week to trend higher as confidence in timing and storm\ntrack increases. Heavy rain and possibly some severe weather\npotential may develop pending the overall storm system evolution.",
